    <string name="privacy_threat_model">Privacy details</string>
    <string name="privacy_threat_model_body">1MESSAGES asks Android for SMS access, which means apps with the default SMS role can read your texts. Android protects this data with app sandboxing and device encryption, not with a separate password. App lock stops casual access to the app but cannot hide already-delivered notification content shown by the system. Deleting a conversation removes the local system copy; your carrier or the recipient may still have it.</string>

